  "steps": [
    "In a medium saucepan, combine the dry long-grain white rice, chicken broth, and 1/4 tsp of the salt. Bring to a boil over medium-high heat, then cover, reduce heat to low, and simmer for 15 minutes until liquid is absorbed and rice is tender and fluffy.",
    "In a small bowl, mix the chili powder, ground cumin, garlic powder, and 1 teaspoon of the salt together.",
    "Toss the diced chicken breast pieces with 1 tablespoon of olive oil and the spice mix until evenly coated.",
    "Heat the remaining 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a 12-inch skillet over medium-high heat. Add the seasoned chicken in a single layer and cook undisturbed for 4 to 5 minutes, then stir and cook for another 3 to 4 minutes until golden brown and the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C).",
    "In a separate small bowl, whisk together the plain non-fat Greek yogurt, fresh lime juice, and the remaining 1/4 tsp of salt to create the crema.",
    "Divide the cooked rice evenly among 4 bowls, top with the warm spiced chicken, black beans, corn, and a drizzle of the Greek yogurt crema."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Swap white rice for brown rice or quinoa for extra fiber.",
    "Store components in airtight containers in the refrigerator for up to 4 days.",
    "Add freshly chopped cilantro or diced jalapeños for extra flavor."
  ],
  "storage": "Store in airtight meal prep containers in the refrigerator for up to 4 days. Keep the Greek yogurt crema in a separate small container until ready to reheat and eat.",
